---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../lib/site-path.mjs";
---

<DocsLayout title="Install — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Install</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Prerequisites: <code>mise</code>, Git, and an authenticated coding harness
      available on the execution host. Setup installs the other dependencies
      locally through mise. On a Mac without mise, install it through your
      normal package manager first (<code>brew install mise</code>).
    </p>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Install and launch</h2>
      <p>Stage the runtime, explicitly start your selected HC core, then launch the coordinator:</p>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>git clone https://github.com/douglasjarquin/sum.git</div>
        <div class="c"># Start the selected HC core explicitly using its matched manual.</div>
        <div class="c"># In the clone:</div>
        <div>cd /path/to/sum</div>
        <div>mise trust</div>
        <div>mise run setup</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl coordinator start --socket /absolute/path/to/hc.sock --session sum --hc-config-home /absolute/path/to/hc-config --harness codex</div>
      </div>
      <p>Setup stages exact HC 0.1.14 and its matched manual/template. Observation never starts a core. <code>coordinator start</code> records the bound launch environment and matching initialization receipt; without qualified HC context, <code>init</code> defaults to developer.</p>
      <p style="margin:14px 0 0">Read the exact procedure path returned by <code>init</code>. An existing qualified terminal needs explicit coordinator initialization and records a known launch or explicitly unknown model; never guess an exact model through <code>--same-as-you</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Recommended harnesses</h2>
      <p>Automatic input is qualified for Codex 0.166.0 with its default keymap and Sum’s namespaced HC Tab-submit template. Other harnesses require actual qualification evidence. Keep normal trust and permission gates; fresh setup generates no custom Sum MCP server and preserves unrelated integrations.</p>
      <p>
        Harness choice, model flags, and presets are in <a
          href={sitePath("configuration")}>Configuration</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>No installed harness?</h2>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>mise run setup -- --install-codex</div>
        <div>mise exec -- codex             <span class="c"># authenticate using the normal provider flow</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>An explicitly requested optional Codex install is local to <code>.deps/harnesses</code>. No account, subscription or global configuration is created or switched. Setup alone does not qualify an authenticated harness.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Talk to it</h2>
      <p>Then delegate normally:</p>
      <blockquote style="margin-bottom:14px">
        Use Codex to fix the failing login test in <code style="font-size:13px"
          >/Users/me/projects/myapp</code
        >. Keep scope to the bug, run the existing checks, arrange independent
        review, and bring me a PR. Do not merge it. Ask before changing the
        public API.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        The coordinator creates a task brief, prepares a separate Git
        worktree, launches the selected worker, submits its brief, and returns
        control to you. Every session starts with <code>./bin/sumctl init</code>
        and follows the role it returns.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
